{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Bounded Agentic Checkout — Agent Commerce Interface",
    "version": "2.1.0",
    "description": "x402 V2 wire-format conformance pass: PAYMENT-REQUIRED / PAYMENT-SIGNATURE / PAYMENT-RESPONSE headers, CAIP-2-shaped network identifiers, GET /agent/v1/discovery, the formal x402 Extensions mechanism (extensions.info/schema), PaymentPayload.accepted (the full chosen PaymentRequirements object — the previous v2.0.0 draft of this spec had this wrong, a real gap found and fixed in this revision, see docs/x402-conformance-diff.md), and 402 (not 404) for payment-settlement failures. Every CatalogItem also carries settlement_type: \"fiat\" directly. This spec is versioned alongside, not overwriting, the frozen Phase 4a/4b v1.0.1 spec at docs/agent-commerce-interface.openapi.json — v1 clients are still served by the same running backend. Full field-by-field reference, the live diff checklist, and the honesty-boundary discussion live in docs/x402-conformance-diff.md, docs/x402-v2-conformance.md, and docs/agent-commerce-catalog-README.md; this file is the current spec's machine-readable shape.\n\nSettlement is processed via Razorpay (India, fiat, test-mode). This is not an onchain settlement network. network values under the inr-fiat: prefix are a documented x402 extension for this deployment, not part of the core x402 network registry."
  },
